      "title": "Master–Micro Residual Correction With Adaptive Tactile Fusion and Force-Mixed Control for Contact-Rich Manipulation",
      "takeaway": "This paper addresses contact-rich, fine-grained manipulation, where visual imitation learning misses cues such as friction variation and incipient slip and struggles to balance long-horizon coherence with local reactive feedback. M2-ResiPolicy pairs a 10 Hz Master-Guidance Policy that generates action chunks from a diffusion-based backbone and uses tactile-intensity-driven adaptive fusion to modulate vision-touch perceptual weights with a 60 Hz Micro-Residual Corrector, a lightweight GRU producing real-time compensation from TCP wrench feedback, plus a force-mixed PBIC execution layer. The abstract reports that across fragile grasping and precision insertion tasks it outperforms standard Diffusion Policy (DP) and Reactive Diffusion Policy (RDP), reaching a 93% damage-free success rate in chip grasping with stable force regulation. Inspect how the adaptive tactile fusion weights are computed and how the two timescales are coordinated.",
