      "title": "Sim-to-Real Learning for Humanoid Box Loco-Manipulation",
      "takeaway": "This work targets humanoid box loco-manipulation, which requires whole-body coordination to lift boxes of varying weight, position, and orientation while maintaining balance. The authors present a sim-to-real reinforcement learning approach that trains general box pickup and carrying skills for the bipedal robot Digit, with reward functions designed to shape the desired box interactions while valuing balance and gait quality, and they combine the learned skills into a full system for moving boxes between tables. Beyond quantitative simulation results, the abstract reports successful sim-to-real transfer on Digit and states that, to the authors' knowledge, this is the first demonstration of a learned controller for such a task on real hardware. Inspect the reward design and skill composition.",
